{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/203372-modern-paganism-wicca-and-other-mystics-what-important-topics-get-ignored","id":203372,"title":"Modern Paganism, Wicca, and other mystics what important topics get ignored?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-20T18:59:01-07:00","id":203372,"title":"Modern Paganism, Wicca, and other mystics what important topics get ignored?","content":"So what important topics get ignored? If not ignored not given enough emphasis? Or is often not found in beginner/ multi topic books? <br /> <br /> To clear up the question. <br /> <br /> On other sites when this question gets asked they usually say Centering and Grounding is too important to not be given more emphasis but acknowledge only so much can be babbled about in a book before it gets arrogant in the sense. &quot;I can't believe you dont know how to do that but lets fill a page at you with a few excersises with out explaining why they are good.&quot; <br /> <br /> Not so much a post about general Neo Paganism or Wicca or other groups. But from those who are, have some back ground in the topics and feel comfortable saying so. What would be topics that should be added to the new to Paganism books or beginner books. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","user":"BellaFeylin","date":".  No one understood the OP. 07-21-2014, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","name":"BellaFeylin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:20:19-07:00","id":203413,"title":"","content":"*nods*<br /> Doing some reading; <a href=\"http://www.cbn.com/entertainment/books/elliottb_wicca.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">Wicca Fastest Growing Religion</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.examiner.com/article/is-the-pagan-religion-taking-over-America\" target=\"_blank\">Is Paganism Slowly Taking over America?</a><br /> <br /> All taking with a grain of salt these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:33:54-07:00","id":203417,"title":"","content":"That has nothing to do with my question unless you are trying to say that the growth is worth mentioning and explaining?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","user":"BellaFeylin","date":". 07-20-2014, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","name":"BellaFeylin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:37:31-07:00","id":203425,"title":"","content":"The thread title inspired me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:01:09-07:00","id":203554,"title":"","content":"Firstly, thank you to the OP for bringing up &quot;alternative&quot; religions and the concept of modern paganism in it's very own thread.<br /> <br /> ..And that's where you lose me. There are countless issues being ignored, glossed over or simply not given the emphasis or attention they deserve.<br /> <br /> Is this the new Religion thread?<br /> Is this the Mysticism and Occult thread?<br /> WHAT BOOKS ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?<br /> <br /> So many questions....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:15:41-07:00","id":203562,"title":"","content":"Philosophically Curious Child: Dad?<br /> Dad: Yes, mein progeny?<br /> PCC: Can you really just lump together just about every human belief since we, as a species, started recording our ignorance based, fear induced illogical beliefs and suspicions in one thread?<br /> Dad: Probably not. <br /> <br /> *Dad smirks*<br /> <br /> PCC: What is it, Dad?<br /> Dad: What's the sound of one hand fapping?<br /> PCC: Hehe. What? I have no idea. What is it?<br /> Dad: Your sister snoring.<br /> PCC: What the...? I DON'T HAVE A SISTER.<br /> Dad: Exactly. Wrap it up or rub it out until you're 18, Billy. <br /> <br /> *Dad then transforms into a swan and flies off to shag Billy's mom.*<br /> <br /> Religion is weird. Mythology is weirder. Human beings are the weirdest of all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 07-21-2014, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T06:55:22-07:00","id":203806,"title":"","content":"Az, I think you have just summed up every attempt at a religion thread on this forum since the White Wolf forms were created.<br /> <br /> <b>BRILLIANT!!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T06:57:35-07:00","id":203810,"title":"","content":"Which topics aren't in the beginner books that should be or are in but aren't handled well?<br /> <br /> This is not a general other religion topic but a thread for the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","user":"BellaFeylin","date":". 07-21-2014, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","name":"BellaFeylin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:03:46-07:00","id":203815,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the question","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:28:52-07:00","id":203831,"title":"","content":"I sort of do, but I have some worries about how far this might go.<br /> <br /> As a minor answer, I gotta say that it's tough to declare what some people should learn immediately going into the various strictures because the entire damn thing is vague as hell. Nevermind that the old religions aren't really codified in a way a lot of Western spiritualists are set to understand easily, and that therefore the entire definition of them and their crafts becomes immensely fuzzy and diverse(without even touching on neo-paganism), and nevermind that the people writing books have their own opinions about what's good opening fodder for initiates and beginners-the entire subject is very in tune with the idea of the individual's rate of progression, so some people are ready for more, some for less, some for certain subjects and not for others.<br /> <br /> As a general rule though, the philosophy and attitudes and broad metaphysical viewpoint of each branch of spirituality make for good starting points as a general rule. People who want to know more about the craft can easily build from a good beginner book on their own(although they should really seek out the wise in their community, if there be any).<br /> <br /> I don't think the craft needs to be rushed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And again, all of this is a minor answer because I still don't think the question is particularly clear.<br /> <br /> EDIT:I'm not really sure why I felt like saying something","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-21-2014, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:37:38-07:00","id":203835,"title":"","content":"So, more serious, yeah....the &quot;alt beliefs&quot; don't get a lot of coverage or discussion in mass media in general (and usually when they do, it's not a positive spin) and they really don't get brought up much on here. Don't know how much of that stems from not many OP/WW players being part of the alt beliefs crowd and how much of it simply not feeling the need/not feeling safe to discuss such things openly.<br /> <br /> I know that for myself, it takes me paragraphs to hammer out my personal paradigm which has been cobbled together from sources all over the world. So, it's not exactly something I like to discuss because it takes so much just to explain where I'm coming from and there's so much room for misunderstanding in there as to not make it worth the trouble. I can't point to just one major, widely known and understood religion and say &quot;That one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Makes for a long day of explanation which often makes me feel like I'm having to defend my beliefs. It's hard enough dealing with an absurdist perspective without having to explain it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T08:18:40-07:00","id":203861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BellaFeylin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/203372-modern-paganism-wicca-and-other-mystics-what-important-topics-get-ignored?p=203810#post203810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which topics aren't in the beginner books that should be or are in but aren't handled well?<br /> <br /> This is not a general other religion topic but a thread for the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer this, try <a href=\"http://www.witchvox.com/\" target=\"_blank\">www.witchvox.com</a><br /> <br /> They're going to have a lot more info on this topic than this site.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And isn't it a terrible commentary on American pop culture that I feel weird taking anyone named &quot;Bella&quot; anything seriously?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 07-21-2014, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:16:02-07:00","id":203892,"title":"","content":"Bela Lugosi's dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:54:46-07:00","id":203927,"title":"","content":"Well, the things is, during my search and research for...personal faith, I guess would be the best description, I've noticed that adherence to one religion tends to desire people to render other beliefs null and void, sometimes destructively. Most certainly harmful to progressive ideas and even ideals, that should continue to move and evolve spiritually if possible.<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say that I consider myself to be multi-faceted in regards to religious beliefs. Gnostic, Buddhist, Druid, Witch, Jedi...(yeah sure, it's part of evolving), Animist...I guess I have a lot of beliefs. But, y'know, you have to believe in yourself first to get that nice solid foundation to build upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:48:11-07:00","id":203960,"title":"","content":"Stephenie Meyer ruined it for everyone, Papa Bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:54:06-07:00","id":203967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/203372-modern-paganism-wicca-and-other-mystics-what-important-topics-get-ignored?p=203927#post203927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the things is, during my search and research for...personal faith, I guess would be the best description, I've noticed that adherence to one religion tends to desire people to render other beliefs null and void, sometimes destructively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of them.<br /> <br /> One of the things that drew me to a lot of Eastern religions/philosophies was this little story, it's got a lot of version, but here's a short one.<br /> <br /> Three blind men walk up to an elephant to find out what it's like.<br /> The first one touches the leg and proclaims, &quot;An elephant is like a tree.&quot;<br /> The second one touches the ear and proclaims, &quot;An elephant is like a sail.&quot;<br /> The third one touches the trunk and proclaims, &quot;An elephant is like a snake.&quot;<br /> The three men walk away arguing about how the others are wrong.<br /> <br /> MORAL: They're all wrong because what they're trying to proclaim as the truth is just one tiny piece of the whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T11:24:35-07:00","id":203992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/203372-modern-paganism-wicca-and-other-mystics-what-important-topics-get-ignored?p=203960#post203960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stephenie Meyer ruined it for everyone, Papa Bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had to talk a friend of mine out of naming her daughter &quot;Isabella&quot;. She comes from a long line of Italians and there has been an Isabella in almost every generation in her family. She'd never heard of those blasted books so she had no idea her girl would be one of probably 10 &quot;Bella&quot;s in her class in school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T11:34:00-07:00","id":204002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/203372-modern-paganism-wicca-and-other-mystics-what-important-topics-get-ignored?p=203967#post203967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the things that drew me to a lot of Eastern religions/philosophies was this little story, it's got a lot of version, but here's a short one.<br /> <br /> Three blind men walk up to an elephant to find out what it's like.<br /> The first one touches the leg and proclaims, &quot;An elephant is like a tree.&quot;<br /> The second one touches the ear and proclaims, &quot;An elephant is like a sail.&quot;<br /> The third one touches the trunk and proclaims, &quot;An elephant is like a snake.&quot;<br /> The three men walk away arguing about how the others are wrong.<br /> <br /> MORAL: They're all wrong because what they're trying to proclaim as the truth is just one tiny piece of the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The best version is in Clanbook: Malkavian. Just saying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T19:35:39-07:00","id":204545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/203372-modern-paganism-wicca-and-other-mystics-what-important-topics-get-ignored?p=203967#post203967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all of them.<br /> <br /> One of the things that drew me to a lot of Eastern religions/philosophies was this little story, it's got a lot of version, but here's a short one.<br /> <br /> Three blind men walk up to an elephant to find out what it's like.<br /> The first one touches the leg and proclaims, &quot;An elephant is like a tree.&quot;<br /> The second one touches the ear and proclaims, &quot;An elephant is like a sail.&quot;<br /> The third one touches the trunk and proclaims, &quot;An elephant is like a snake.&quot;<br /> The three men walk away arguing about how the others are wrong.<br /> <br /> MORAL: They're all wrong because what they're trying to proclaim as the truth is just one tiny piece of the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods*<br /> <br /> A personal favorite of mine is from Sufism; Slightly different versions, but more importantly, different ways to interpret;<br /> <u>The Lost Key</u><br /> <i>The great Sufi master Mullah Nasruddin was on his hands and knees searching for something under a streetlamp. A man saw him and asked, &quot;What are you looking for?&quot; &quot;My house key,&quot; Nasruddin replied. &quot;I lost it.&quot; The man joined him in looking for the key, and after a period of fruitless searching, the man asked, &quot;Are you sure you lost it around here?&quot; Nasruddin replied, &quot;Oh, I didn't lose it around here. I lost it over there, by my house.&quot; &quot;Then why,&quot; the man asked, &quot;are you looking for it over here?&quot; &quot;Because,&quot; Nasruddin said, &quot;The light is so much better over here.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:12:34-07:00","id":204964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=